    <briefdescription>
<para>Method processing, FPGA/AFE control, and probe orchestration. </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><heading level="1">TinyProbe Module</heading>
</para><para>TinyProbe translates incoming control messages into hardware actions on the probe. It owns the method registry, FPGA/AFE access, and buffers that feed outbound data paths.</para><para><heading level="2">Architecture</heading>
</para><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Method dispatch: protobuf request decoding and routing in <ref refid="tp__methods_8h" kindref="compound">tp_methods.h</ref></para></listitem><listitem><para>Method handlers: grouped under <ref refid="group__tinyprobe__methods" kindref="compound">TinyProbe Methods</ref> with one handler per generated method</para></listitem><listitem><para>Hardware control: FPGA, AFE, TX, mux, and power accessors in <ref refid="tp__fpga_8h" kindref="compound">tp_fpga.h</ref>, <ref refid="tp__afe_8h" kindref="compound">tp_afe.h</ref>, <ref refid="tp__tx_8h" kindref="compound">tp_tx.h</ref>, <ref refid="tp__mux_8h" kindref="compound">tp_mux.h</ref>, and <ref refid="tp__power_8h" kindref="compound">tp_power.h</ref></para></listitem><listitem><para>Buffering: circular buffer helpers in <ref refid="tp__buffer_8h" kindref="compound">tp_buffer.h</ref></para></listitem></itemizedlist>
</para><para><heading level="2">Data Flow (high level)</heading>
</para><para><orderedlist>
<listitem><para>WiUS transport receives a message and forwards it to the TinyProbe method layer.</para></listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput><ref refid="tp__methods_8c_1ab763b48bb0caae51d13d3a8b9d417311" kindref="member">tp_methods_handle()</ref></computeroutput> decodes the nanopb request and selects the matching handler from <ref refid="group__tinyprobe__methods" kindref="compound">TinyProbe Methods</ref>.</para></listitem><listitem><para>Handlers perform register writes/reads through TinyProbe helpers and may enqueue data into probe buffers.</para></listitem><listitem><para>Status replies are encoded as protobuf responses and returned via the WiUS transport.</para></listitem></orderedlist>
</para><para><heading level="2">Extending TinyProbe</heading>
</para><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Add a new method: update the generated method definition, create <computeroutput>tp_method_&lt;name&gt;.c/.h</computeroutput>, add it to <computeroutput>TP_METHODS</computeroutput>, and document it under <ref refid="group__tinyprobe__methods" kindref="compound">TinyProbe Methods</ref>.</para></listitem><listitem><para>Touch hardware safely: prefer helper APIs in <computeroutput>tp_fpga</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>tp_afe</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>tp_tx</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>tp_mux</computeroutput>, and <computeroutput>tp_power</computeroutput> rather than open-coded register writes to keep side effects contained. </para></listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>    </detaileddescription>
